From 88e39870a7f94e921d687ebc7b917dd8e1dedf35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elvis kahoro <github@elvis.ai>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:37:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tabular_data_preview: Open Parquet files in the table view

Parquet is binary, so the text-buffer path rejects it with "Binary files
are not supported" before the CSV preview can see it. Claim .parquet as
a project item instead, decode it off the main thread with the parquet
crate (row API, no arrow), and feed the result to the existing TableView
so sorting and filtering work unchanged.

Decoding stops at 100,000 rows and the view says how many were shown.
Files over 512 MB, or whose previewed row groups would decompress past
1 GB per the footer, are refused because the whole file is read before
decoding. The view re-reads the file when it changes on disk, keeping
the last good rows if the new contents fail to decode. Remote worktrees
can't load binary files yet, so they are left to the default handler.
